# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The studio's raw photo library, uploaded straight to the repo root: 86 files,
# ~30 MB, plus the stray `תמונות`. It is source material for tools/*.mjs — the
# slot -> filename map is tools/manifest.json — and every derivative the site
# actually serves is committed under assets/img/. A leading slash anchors each
# pattern to the root, so assets/img/*.jpg and assets/img/*.webp are untouched.
#
# .vercelignore carries the same list and is what keeps these off the CDN.
# This file is the other half: it keeps them out of HEAD, so a future edit to
# .vercelignore cannot turn the repo into a public archive of the studio's
# work, and the deploy tarball stops carrying 30 MB nobody requests.
#
# Adding a pattern here does NOTHING to a file git already tracks. The
# load-bearing step is `git rm --cached` — see DEPLOY.md.
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.heic
/תמונות

# Scratch worktrees from agent sessions.
.claude/worktrees/

# Local Claude Code permission grants — machine-scoped, never a repo-wide standing grant
.claude/settings.local.json

# Images dropped at the repo root. check.sh already fails on them — "אין
# תמונות גולמיות ב-HEAD" — but it runs here, and GitHub's web uploader does
# not: a master dropped through `Add file` → `Upload files` went straight to
# main and left it red until someone happened to run the checks locally.
# This is the second layer, so the mistake cannot be committed in the first
# place. Everything the site serves lives under assets/.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
